{
  "id": "samba_de_bumbo",
  "name": "Samba de bumbo (rural samba of São Paulo)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Rural samba of the São Paulo interior described by Mário de Andrade in his study O samba rural paulista, closely tied to the August pilgrimage festival of Bom Jesus at Pirapora do Bom Jesus, where black sambadores from across the state gathered; groups continue in Pirapora and Santana de Parnaíba, and a related samba campineiro belongs to Campinas. A large bumbo bass drum leads the samba, joined by caixa and chocalhos, while a leader raises short sung verses that the group repeats as the dancers follow the drum. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the bumbo and a generic shaker card for the chocalhos.",
  "recipe": "classic modern samba de bumbo, groove Percussion, Brazilian branch. single leader group response. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane snare drum, shaker source unspecified. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
